Negative control for the per-panel stage (RT1).

The stage is where a mounted collection offers the controls a hand would press.
On an area's page several collections are mounted at once (Links and Referrals
both draw a Refresh), so each panel holds its own stage and a step presses the
panel it booted. This mutant puts every panel back on the one shared stage: the
last collection to mount wins, a step meant for Links presses Referrals' Refresh,
and `remove` / `edit` are looked for on a collection that never drew them.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected red (unit lane): world-cells.spec.ts — a press made through a world
built under one panel namespace must reach that panel's collection and never a
sibling's.

